A||N||16||Voytek||3.1 Injectors - Any Power Increase In A Bored Out 2.8?||||1||
Z||000000||Voytek||08-20-2001||02:27 PM||||Ok, here's the question.  I have a 2.8 V6 that isn't a 2.8 anymore - I had it bored out to a 3.1.  I can get some cheap injectors from an aluminum head 3.1.  Would that increase the power?  Is it worth the work? (the price is negligible and I would do the work myself).  Would that require any computer mods?<P>Thanks for any info!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||08-20-2001||03:44 PM||||I wouldn't invest in injectors unless you are gonna put later NOS or a Turbo. Stock injectors will do with a 3.1. I have stock in my 3.4 & do just fine.<BR>I'm curious how you got to 3.1 with only a bore increase?||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||08-20-2001||04:06 PM||||I do know that you can not use 3100 injectors.  I don't believe 3.1 injectors are any diff than 2.8.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||08-20-2001||04:18 PM||||How I got to 3.1 with just a bore??<BR>I'm not sure how to answer that other than like this: the cylinders were bored out (I forgot how much over) to accommodate 3.1L pistons (i.e. increased displacement).  What I probably should have got was a 3.1 stroker kit.  Oh well...||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||04:29 PM||||If you want more fuel flow to keep up, invest in an adjustable fuel pressure regulator... kick up your flow a little bit.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||Voytek||08-20-2001||04:39 PM||||Hey MinnGreenGt<BR>What kind of 3.1 do you have (heads, year, etc.)?  I was originally going to put an aluminum head 3.1 in my Fiero but the shop discrouraged me from doing it 'cause they didn't have any experience with that.  I'm kinda kicking myself now.  Is it a pretty good increase in power from a 2.8?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||05:03 PM||||Voytek- The 3.1 Block is from a late model (year unsure) Chevy Lumina Minivan (Pontiac Transport).  The heads are original Fiero 2.8 that have been ported and polished to increase flow. Additionally the Throttlbody & Intake plenum have been bored out (courtsey of Darrell Morse), as well as a ported exhaust manifold and free-flow exhaust (High-Flow Cat & Baffle tips.  No muffler!)  I haven't gotten the adjustable fuel pressure regulator yet- but am planning on getting it shortly! Let me know if you have any other Q's... I'll tell you whatever I can come up with!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000007||Voytek||08-20-2001||05:16 PM||||Got it.  I had my 2.8 bored out with 3.1 pistons, performance cam (Federal Mogul) and Sprint headers (no cat).  I have to say, the difference in performance from my original 2.8 is NOT huge.  I mean, the car is definitely faster but I was expecting much more, hence I am asking about the 3.1 injectors.  I actually HAD a 3.1 from a '91 TransSport (iron heads) but it had a bunch of caked oil in the heads - I returned it.  I also had a 3.1 aluminum head from a '91 Lumina car.  Very nice looking engine with low mileage and I've seen these in Fieros before.  Should have gone with it.  I realize the look would not be stock but it's not like my car looks stock anywhere else.<P>I guess what I'm concerned with is this.  I had the engine bored out BUT, the heads were shaved too.  All in all, am I virtually back to the 2.8 displacement, i.e. larger cyl. diameter but longer piston travel, hence no change in compression?  Does that make sense?||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||05:49 PM||||I'm not totally sure about the difference in compression... have you checked it and compare to stock? If you have longer travel, and shaved heads, you should have a higher compression ratio? I think...?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000009||Voytek||08-20-2001||05:58 PM||||Theoretically, yes, BUT the pistons are larger (3.1), so it would make sense that this would reduce the compression, right?  It's just something that's been bugging me for a while now.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||08-20-2001||06:14 PM||||If you used 3.1 liter pistons your compression should be quite a bit lower as the wrist pin locations are different in the 3.1 pistons. Without changing the crank the 3.1 pistons won't travel as far up in the cylinder. I'm sure someone else has the numbers but I think the biggest difference twist the 2.8 and the 3.1 is the stroke. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Voytek||08-20-2001||06:26 PM||||Ok.  I guess I should clarify this.  I did use the 3.1 crank and pistons (or at least that's what the shop tells me).  I see what you're getting at (I think) - the 3.1 crank should ensure that I get that slightly higher compression that is lost with a 3.1 bore, right?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Shaun41178||08-20-2001||07:52 PM||||ok some of you aren't understanding that the 3.1 piston is not necessarily an overbore piston.<P>From the factory the 2.8 and 3.1 has the same bore.  Its the stroke that is different<P>Stop Calling it a 3.1 bore!!<P>It would be 3.1 iron head pistons with a 3.1 crank would be the right way to say it.  You guys are confusing each other and yourselves cause you don't know what you are talking about and using different terms to try and describe what you think you are talking about.  Increasing bore without changing anything else technically raises the compresson ratio not lowers it.<P>Why is it when all you people do the 3.1 builds none of you have your machinist check the compression ratio for you?  Formula88 had to plug the numbers into a computer to come with the ratio numbers.  If you had your machinist do this he would have given you all the numbers of the chamber and dish of the piston and calculated it all for you and tell you what it is.  Then none of you would have to guess.  Then you could come on the forum here and say that with this much shaved off the deck and this much off the heads with this piston and this gasket I got "x" compression ratio.  Then people could guesstimate what theirs would be based of this info.<P>It amazes me how many of you have done the 3.1 conversion but none have bothered to have the compression calculated.  And then some of you wonder why it seems like it runs sluggish.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||08-20-2001||07:54 PM||||oh yea you dont' need 3.1 injectors.  your 2.8 ones can flow enough.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Voytek2||08-20-2001||10:21 PM||||Thanks for the answer and clarification Shaun41178, even if it was a bit snappy.||||reg||1
